.TH LOCATED 1 "2025-02-06" "0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
located \- device location tracking server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B located
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B located
is a lightweight HTTP server for registering and locating mobile devices.
It stores device registrations in a SQLite database, sends push notifications
via FCM (Android) and APNs (iOS) to trigger location lookups, and returns
GPS coordinates in real time. No location history is stored.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR daemon ", " \-d
Start the HTTP server in the foreground.
Blocks until SIGINT or SIGTERM is received.
.TP
.B devices
List all registered devices.
Requires a running daemon; uses curl to query the API.
.TP
.BI locate " id"
Request location of the device with the given
.IR id .
Sends a push notification to the device and waits for a GPS response.
Requires a running daemon.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR version ", " \-v
Print version and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " path"
Path to the JSON configuration file.
May appear anywhere in the argument list.
Default: uses built-in defaults (port 8080, db ./devices.db).
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file is JSON with the following keys:
.TP
.B listen_port
TCP port for the HTTP server (default: 8080).
.TP
.B db_path
Path to the SQLite database file (default: ./devices.db).
.TP
.B api_key
API key for authenticating admin endpoints (devices, locate).
If not set, admin endpoints are open.
.TP
.B server_url
Public URL of the server, sent to devices in push notifications
so they can POST their location back.
.TP
.B locate_timeout
Seconds to wait for a device to respond with its location (default: 30).
.TP
.B fcm.project_id
Firebase project ID for sending Android push notifications.
.TP
.B fcm.service_account_key_path
Path to the Firebase service account JSON key file.
.TP
.B apns.key_path
Path to the APNs authentication key (.p8 file).
.TP
.B apns.key_id
APNs key ID (10-character string from Apple Developer portal).
.TP
.B apns.team_id
Apple Developer Team ID.
.TP
.B apns.bundle_id
App bundle identifier.
.TP
.B apns.use_sandbox
Use the APNs sandbox environment (default: true).
Set to false for production.
.SH API ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B POST /api/register
Register a new device. JSON body must include
.BR id ", " token ", and " platform
(android or ios).
Optional:
.BR name .
Returns the device record including a generated
.BR secret .
The secret must be included in location callbacks via the
.B X-Device-Secret
header.
.TP
.B DELETE /api/register/<id>
Unregister a device by its id.
.TP
.B GET /api/devices
List all registered devices as a JSON array.
Requires
.B Authorization: Bearer <api_key>
header if api_key is configured.
.TP
.B POST /api/locate/<id>
Trigger a locate request. Sends a push notification to the device,
waits up to
.B locate_timeout
seconds for the device to respond with GPS coordinates.
Returns the location as JSON or a timeout error.
Requires
.B Authorization: Bearer <api_key>
header if api_key is configured.
.TP
.B POST /api/location/<id>
Device callback endpoint. The device POSTs its GPS coordinates
after receiving a push notification. JSON body must include
.BR request_id ", " lat ", and " lng .
Optional:
.BR accuracy .
Requires
.B X-Device-Secret
header matching the device's secret.
.SH SECURITY
.TP
Admin endpoints
.RB ( /api/devices ", " /api/locate )
require an API key in the
.B Authorization: Bearer
header when
.B api_key
is set in the config.
.TP
Device callback
.RB ( /api/location )
requires the device secret in the
.B X-Device-Secret
header.
.TP
Run behind a reverse proxy (nginx, caddy) for TLS termination in production.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/located.json
Default configuration file location (if no \-c given, built-in defaults are used).
.TP
.I ./devices.db
Default SQLite database location.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid arguments, config parse failure, database error, etc.).
.SH KNOWN LIMITATIONS
.TP
.B iOS force-quit
If the user swipes the app away, silent pushes will not wake it.
.TP
.B Aggressive Android OEMs
Xiaomi, Huawei, and some Samsung models kill background services.
Users may need to disable battery optimization.
.TP
.B No offline queuing
If the device is off or has no internet, the request times out.
.TP
.B GPS cold start
First fix after a long time can take 15\-30 seconds.
.SH AUTHORS
Written for the allardtrac project.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
